This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net.  Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[2]: Scrolls of remove curse should resist cursing. Rings of fire
resistance (if wooden) should resist burning. Rings of shock resistance
should resist lightning. - azgor

[3]: Striking Medusa in melee with an edged weapon should occasionally
produce one or more snakes on adjacent squares.  "My hair!" - azgor

[4]: Miswritten scrolls (perhaps written while confused or
hallucinated, or some other means) - automatically behave as though
you're confused when reading them.  Reading one when confused gives the
originally intended effect. - Grunt

[5]: If you have levitation, you should be able to dig upwards. -
ChocoCid

[6]: new commestible: a fruitcake.  It counts as fruit so can be eaten
by horses, etc.  It is very heavy.  It takes a long time to eat.  And
it gives an obscene amount of nutrition.  If you ate an entire
fruitcake IRL, it would take you all day to do it and you wouldn't eat
again for a week. - azgor

[7]: Conflict should only affect the same subset of monsters that
Elbereth does. - doy

[8]: Blowing a non-cursed magic whistle while confused should levelport
pets to you.  Blowing a cursed magic whistle while confused should
teleport monsters to you. - azgor

[9]: According to Die Zauberflote, a magic flute will make hostile men
and beasts become happy (peaceful?) and will protect the user from the
ordeal of fire and the ordeal of water (the elemental planes?).  So
shouldn't ours?  It should be an artifact and it should be tempered by
having limited charges. - azgor

[10]: You should be able to rape foocubi.  This should give you a
penalty if you're lawful, and a bonus if you're chaotic. - ChocoCid

[11]: Boulders falling from the sky (scroll of earth) should have a
chance of destroying any fragile object it lands on (not ones carried
by monsters, however) - Cid|Slp

[12]: You can roll boulders over tiny monsters. Squelch. Or under
flying ones. - ek|M

[13]: In the begining prompt for your race, role, gender and alignment,
NetHack should also ask if you want a cat, dog, horse, or no pet. -
HappyFoppy

[14]: The Vafer theen mint, when consumed - if you'd choke to death,
you explode instead. Cannot lifesave. Posessions are spread over a wide
area, and not cursed (as you die very shorly afterwards. Oh sir... just
one. - SpeedEvil

[15]: Actually, any death by explosion (wand explosion, land mines,
etc) or other means of violent discorporation should scatter your
possessions randomly in a 5-square radius.  :) Possibly also scatter
some meatballs around. - lorimer

[16]: Acidic corpses (and potions of acid) should occasionally
hallucinate instead, with the message "You are now on a very bad acid
trip." - Grunt

[17]: Walking over a potion of acid, while wielding a cockatrice,
should have the same effect as tripping down stairs. (An acid trip.) -
SpeedEvil

